We need a smarter approach. Let's think about when a rotation of P equals sorted.

Sorted = [0, 1, 2, ..., n-1].

rotate_left(P, k) = sorted means P[k], P[k+1], ..., P[n-1], P[0], ..., P[k-1] = [0, 1, ..., n-1].

This means P[i] = (i - k) mod n for all i. In other words, P[i] ≡ i - k (mod n), or P[i] - i ≡ -k (mod n).

So we need P[i] - i to be constant (mod n) for all i, and that constant is -k mod n.

